failure_location.quote:
Let $(h_k)_k$ be bounded and satisfy $\step_k<\dissi_{\tau(t_k)}/\lip_{\tau(t_k)}^2$. Then it holds
    \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{k\rightarrow\infty}\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\step_i\prod_{j=i+1}^{k-1}\left(1 - 2 \step_j \dissi_{\tau(t_j)} + 2\lip_{\tau(t_j)}^2\step_j^2\right)<\infty.
    \end{equation}
